    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Adds a dashboard metabox that allows a user to quickly find and edit specific core or custom blocks across all post types on a site.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to your /wp-content/plugins/ folder.</li>\n<li>Go to the <strong>Plugins</strong> page and activate the plugin.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='how%20do%20i%20use%20this%20plugin%3F'>\nHow do I use this plugin?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<ol>\n<li>Once activated head to the dashboard</li>\n<li>Look for the &#8220;Block Finder&#8221; item</li>\n<li>Select your post type and block</li>\n<li>Click &#8220;Find Block&#8221;</li>\n</ol>\n</p>\n<dt id='how%20to%20uninstall%20the%20plugin%3F'>\nHow to uninstall the plugin?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Simply deactivate and delete the plugin.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<p>View the <a href=\"https://github.com/troychaplin/block-finder/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">changelog</a> in the Github repo.</p>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Easily find content blocks anywhere on your site.",
